From 0e043fb68ac2d23e024fb9fe273f75859814d784 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:12:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] ASoC: soc-core: Start the runtime component count at zero

Since commit 4dd10fbbeb9c ("treewide: Convert devm_kmalloc() family to
the devm_kmalloc_obj() family"), soc_new_pcm_runtime() allocates the
runtime with devm_kzalloc_flex(). When the compiler has
__builtin_counted_by_ref() (GCC 16, for example), that sets
num_components, the __counted_by() counter of components[], to the size
of the array.

snd_soc_rtd_add_component() then appends after those empty slots, and
for_each_rtd_components() stops at the first, empty, one, so no
component of the link is probed. Binding the card then dereferences the
unset card of a component's DAPM context:

  Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at virtual address 0000000000000060
  pc : mutex_lock+0x14/0x68
  lr : snd_soc_dapm_add_routes+0x34/0xa8
  Call trace:
   mutex_lock+0x14/0x68 (P)
   hdmi_dai_probe+0xb0/0x1e0
   snd_soc_pcm_dai_probe+0x70/0x100
   snd_soc_bind_card+0x5e0/0xc30
   ...
   vc4_hdmi_bind+0x6d8/0x908

Seen on a Raspberry Pi 5 with a kernel built by GCC 16.2. Set the count
back to zero after the allocation: the components are counted as they
are added.

Fixes: 4dd10fbbeb9c ("treewide: Convert devm_kmalloc() family to the devm_kmalloc_obj() family")
Signed-off-by: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
---
 sound/soc/soc-core.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/soc-core.c b/sound/soc/soc-core.c
index fdfd48878..bb67c1461 100644
--- a/sound/soc/soc-core.c
+++ b/sound/soc/soc-core.c
@@ -388,6 +388,14 @@ static struct snd_soc_pcm_runtime *soc_new_pcm_runtime(
 		return NULL;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * devm_kzalloc_flex() sets num_components to the size of the array
+	 * when the compiler has __builtin_counted_by_ref(), but the array is
+	 * empty: snd_soc_rtd_add_component() counts the components as it adds
+	 * them.
+	 */
+	rtd->num_components = 0;
+
 	rtd->dev = dev;
 	INIT_LIST_HEAD(&rtd->list);
 	for_each_pcm_streams(stream) {
-- 
